WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:00.042
23.976

2
00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:11.358
<i>Who am I? You sure you want to know?</i>

3
00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:14.820
<i>The story of my life
is not for the faint of heart.</i>

4
00:03:14.987 --> 00:03:17.614
<i>If somebody said
it was a happy little tale...</i>

5
00:03:17.823 --> 00:03:22.286
<i>if somebody told you I was just an
average guy, not a care in the world...</i>

6
00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:24.246
<i>somebody lied.</i>

7
00:03:25.122 --> 00:03:28.709
<i>But let me assure you, this,
like any story worth telling...</i>

8
00:03:28.876 --> 00:03:30.294
<i>is all about a girl.</i>

9
00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:35.632
<i>That girl. The girl next door.
Mary Jane Watson.</i>

10
00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:38.886
<i>The woman I've loved
since before I liked girls.</i>

11
00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:41.722
<i>I'd like to tell you that's me
next to her.</i>

12
00:03:41.889 --> 00:03:43.891
<i>Aw, heck, I'd even take him.</i>

13
00:03:45.309 --> 00:03:47.811
Hey! Stop the bus!

14
00:03:48.812 --> 00:03:49.980
<i>That's me.</i>

15
00:03:50.189 --> 00:03:52.065
Tell him to stop! Please!

16
00:03:52.274 --> 00:03:53.483
Stop!

17
00:03:53.692 --> 00:03:55.903
Hey! Stop the bus!

18
00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:59.156
Stop! He's been chasing us
since Woodhaven.

19
00:03:59.323 --> 00:04:00.574
Catch a cab, Parker!

20
00:04:05.037 --> 00:04:07.831
Thank you. I'm sorry I'm late.

21
00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.546
What a geek!

22
00:04:15.214 --> 00:04:19.426
- Don't even think about it.
- You're so lame, Parker.

23
00:04:19.593 --> 00:04:21.178
Would you date him?

24
00:04:39.071 --> 00:04:41.281
Midtown High seniors.

25
00:04:41.448 --> 00:04:45.160
No wandering. Proceed direct...
Knock it off.

26
00:04:45.452 --> 00:04:48.914
Remember, it is a privilege
to be here.

27
00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:52.543
We're guests of Columbia University's
Science Department.

28
00:04:52.751 --> 00:04:54.962
So behave accordingly.

29
00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:58.173
Let's not have a repeat
of our trip to the planetarium.

30
00:04:58.382 --> 00:05:00.008
Come on, stay together.

31
00:05:00.175 --> 00:05:03.095
Proceed up the steps
and into the building.

32
00:05:04.263 --> 00:05:07.307
- Where were you?
- Checking out the library.

33
00:05:07.474 --> 00:05:10.018
- Looking at the books.
- Yeah, right.

34
00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.607
- Can we drive around the corner?
- Why?

35
00:05:15.816 --> 00:05:17.609
The entrance is right there.

36
00:05:17.776 --> 00:05:21.488
Dad, this is public school.
I can't show up in a Rolls.

37
00:05:21.697 --> 00:05:24.032
I should trade my car for a Jetta...

38
00:05:24.199 --> 00:05:26.994
because you flunked out
of private school?

39
00:05:27.286 --> 00:05:30.330
- It wasn't for me.
- Of course it was.

40
00:05:30.998 --> 00:05:35.335
- Don't ever be ashamed of who you are.
- I'm not ashamed of who I am.

41
00:05:35.544 --> 00:05:36.837
It's just...

42
00:05:37.004 --> 00:05:38.463
Just what, Harry?

43
00:05:38.672 --> 00:05:40.174
Forget it.

44
00:05:43.177 --> 00:05:44.511
Pete!

45
00:05:44.928 --> 00:05:47.431
- Hi, Harry.
- Hey, man. What's up?

46
00:05:48.307 --> 00:05:50.517
- Won't you be needing this?
- Thanks.

47
00:05:51.476 --> 00:05:55.439
- This is my father, Norman Osborn.
- I've heard so much about you.

48
00:05:55.647 --> 00:05:59.109
- It's an honor, sir.
- Harry says you're a science whiz.

49
00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:02.196
I'm something of a scientist myself.

50
00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:05.532
I read your research
on nanotechnology. Brilliant.

51
00:06:05.699 --> 00:06:08.744
- You understood it?
- Yes, I wrote a paper on it.

52
00:06:08.952 --> 00:06:12.247
Impressive.
Your parents must be very proud.

53
00:06:12.414 --> 00:06:16.960
- I live with my aunt and uncle.
- Hey, you two! Let's move!

54
00:06:17.127 --> 00:06:20.797
- Nice to meet you.
- Hope to see you again.

55
00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:26.637
- He doesn't seem so bad.
- Not if you're a genius.

56
00:06:26.803 --> 00:06:28.764
I think he wants to adopt you.

57
00:06:28.931 --> 00:06:33.644
There are over 32,000 known species
of spider in the world.

58
00:06:33.852 --> 00:06:37.648
<i>They're in the order Araneae,
divided into three suborders.</i>

59
00:06:37.856 --> 00:06:38.941
That's amazing!

60
00:06:39.107 --> 00:06:43.028
This is the most advanced electron
microscope on the East Coast.

61
00:06:43.362 --> 00:06:45.405
It's unreal.

62
00:06:45.572 --> 00:06:48.367
Arachnids from all three
groups possess...

63
00:06:48.575 --> 00:06:52.079
varying strengths
to help them search for food.

64
00:06:52.287 --> 00:06:56.500
<i>For example, the Delena spider,
family Sparassidae...</i>

65
00:06:56.667 --> 00:07:00.838
has the ability to jump
to catch its prey.

66
00:07:01.004 --> 00:07:02.756
For the school paper?

67
00:07:07.261 --> 00:07:12.266
<i>Next, we have the net web spider,
family Filistatidae...</i>

68
00:07:12.474 --> 00:07:14.351
<i>genus Kukulcania.</i>

69
00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:18.939
Spins a funnel-shaped web whose
strands have a tensile strength...

70
00:07:19.147 --> 00:07:24.403
proportionately equal to
the high-tension wires used in Bridges.

71
00:07:24.862 --> 00:07:26.530
- Leave him alone.
- Or what?

72
00:07:26.697 --> 00:07:29.700
Or his father will fire your father.

73
00:07:30.117 --> 00:07:32.452
What's Daddy gonna do? Sue me?

74
00:07:32.619 --> 00:07:35.122
What is going on?

75
00:07:35.289 --> 00:07:38.375
The next person who talks
will fail this course.

76
00:07:38.584 --> 00:07:40.586
- This spider...
- Let's go.

77
00:07:40.752 --> 00:07:44.923
Hunts using reflexes with
nerve-conduction velocity so fast...

78
00:07:45.132 --> 00:07:48.635
that some researchers believe
it borders on precognition.

79
00:07:48.802 --> 00:07:50.971
- An early awareness of danger.
- Jerks.

80
00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.931
A spider-sense.

81
00:07:53.557 --> 00:07:55.225
Hey, look at that spider.

82
00:07:55.392 --> 00:07:59.813
Some spiders change colors
to blend into their environment.

83
00:08:00.063 --> 00:08:01.982
It's a defense mechanism.

84
00:08:02.149 --> 00:08:05.444
Peter, what makes you think
I'd want to know that?

85
00:08:05.611 --> 00:08:06.820
Who wouldn't?

86
00:08:06.987 --> 00:08:10.824
Over five painstaking years,
Columbia's research facility...

87
00:08:10.991 --> 00:08:15.370
- You gonna talk to her now?
- Oh, no. Come on. You talk to her.

88
00:08:15.579 --> 00:08:20.334
With these DNA blueprints, we have
begun what was once thought impossible.

89
00:08:20.542 --> 00:08:24.213
- Disgusting.
- Yeah, hateful little things.

90
00:08:24.421 --> 00:08:25.797
I love them!

91
00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:28.008
Yeah, me too.

92
00:08:28.967 --> 00:08:32.846
You know, spiders can change
their color...

93
00:08:33.013 --> 00:08:36.850
- to blend into their environment.
- Really?

94
00:08:37.017 --> 00:08:41.146
- Yeah, it's a defense mechanism.
- Cool.

95
00:08:41.355 --> 00:08:44.733
Transfer RNA
to encode an entirely new genome...

96
00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:48.028
combining the genetic
information from all three...

97
00:08:48.195 --> 00:08:52.866
into these 15 genetically
designed super-spiders.

98
00:08:53.033 --> 00:08:54.535
There's 14.

99
00:08:54.993 --> 00:08:56.370
I beg your pardon?

100
00:08:56.537 --> 00:08:59.081
- One's missing.
- Yeah.

101
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.628
I guess the researchers
are working on that one.

102
00:09:05.128 --> 00:09:09.842
Do you know that this is the largest
electron microscope on the East Coast?

103
00:09:10.008 --> 00:09:14.096
You were talking throughout
that woman's entire presentation.

104
00:09:14.263 --> 00:09:16.014
Let's talk about listening.

105
00:09:20.102 --> 00:09:24.189
I don't know what it's like
at those fancy private schools...

106
00:09:24.398 --> 00:09:26.275
but at Midtown High...

107
00:09:34.741 --> 00:09:38.495
Could I take your picture?
I need one with a student in it.

108
00:09:38.662 --> 00:09:40.122
- Sure.
- Great.

109
00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.624
Where do you want me?
Over here?

110
00:09:42.833 --> 00:09:44.168
Yeah, that's great.

111
00:09:44.585 --> 00:09:46.253
Don't make me look ugly.

112
00:09:46.628 --> 00:09:48.463
That's impossible.

113
00:09:55.721 --> 00:09:56.972
Perfect.

114
00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.273
- Is that good?
- Great.

115
00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.197
That's great.

116
00:10:18.785 --> 00:10:20.787
M.J., let's go!

117
00:10:22.331 --> 00:10:24.917
Wait. Thanks!

118
00:10:38.388 --> 00:10:41.141
Parker, let's do it.

119
00:10:57.866 --> 00:11:01.328
We've solved the horizon glide
and the balance issues.

120
00:11:01.495 --> 00:11:04.039
I've already seen the glider.

121
00:11:04.456 --> 00:11:06.500
That's not what I'm here for.

122
00:11:06.708 --> 00:11:09.378
General Slocum, good to see you again.

123
00:11:10.212 --> 00:11:12.381
Mr. Balkan, Mr. Fargas.

124
00:11:12.631 --> 00:11:14.466
- Norman.
- Mr. Osborn.

125
00:11:14.633 --> 00:11:18.178
Always a pleasure to have
our board of directors visit.

126
00:11:18.387 --> 00:11:21.807
I want the report on human
performance enhancers.

127
00:11:21.974 --> 00:11:26.478
We tried vapor inhalation with rats.
Their strength increased by 800%.

128
00:11:26.645 --> 00:11:28.522
- Excellent.
- Any side effects?

129
00:11:28.689 --> 00:11:29.773
Once.

130
00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:32.609
All the tests since
have been successful.

131
00:11:32.776 --> 00:11:36.530
In the trial that went wrong,
what were the side effects?

132
00:11:36.697 --> 00:11:39.032
Violence, aggression...

133
00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:40.951
and insanity.

134
00:11:41.118 --> 00:11:43.871
- What do you recommend?
- That was only one test.

135
00:11:44.121 --> 00:11:47.958
Except for Dr. Stromm,
our staff certifies the product...

136
00:11:48.125 --> 00:11:51.044
- ready for human testing.
- Dr. Stromm?

137
00:11:52.379 --> 00:11:56.049
We need to take the whole line
back to formula.

138
00:11:57.301 --> 00:11:59.720
- Back to formula?
- Dr. Osborn.

139
00:12:00.888 --> 00:12:02.723
I'll be frank with you.

140
00:12:02.973 --> 00:12:07.811
I never supported your program. We
have my predecessor to thank for that.

141
00:12:07.978 --> 00:12:10.731
The general has approved
Quest Aerospace...

142
00:12:10.898 --> 00:12:13.817
to build a prototype
of their exoskeleton.

143
00:12:14.151 --> 00:12:18.071
- They test in two weeks.
- And if your performance enhancers...

144
00:12:18.238 --> 00:12:22.326
have not had a successful
human trial by that date...

145
00:12:22.576 --> 00:12:26.955
I'm gonna pull your funding.
I'm going to give it to them.

146
00:12:28.749 --> 00:12:30.417
Gentlemen. Ladies.

147
00:12:35.506 --> 00:12:40.928
And the Lord said, "Let there be light."
And voilà! There is light.

148
00:12:41.178 --> 00:12:43.263
Forty soft, glowing watts of it.

149
00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:48.268
Good boy. God will be thrilled.
Just don't fall on your ass.

150
00:12:48.602 --> 00:12:51.021
I'm already on my ass, May.

151
00:12:51.188 --> 00:12:55.692
When the plant's senior electrician
is laid off after 35 years...

152
00:12:55.859 --> 00:12:58.570
what would you call it?
I am on my ass.

153
00:12:58.779 --> 00:13:01.114
Hand me that dish. The green one.

154
00:13:01.365 --> 00:13:04.117
The corporation is downsizing
the people...

155
00:13:04.576 --> 00:13:06.453
and upsizing their profits.

156
00:13:06.703 --> 00:13:09.623
Oh, Ben, you'll get another job
somewhere.

157
00:13:10.624 --> 00:13:13.544
Well, let's look
in the paper and see.

158
00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:17.464
There are the want ads.
What do we got here?

159
00:13:17.631 --> 00:13:19.258
Computer...

160
00:13:19.466 --> 00:13:23.220
Computer salesman, computer engineer,
computer analyst.

161
00:13:23.387 --> 00:13:27.140
My Lord, even the computers
need analysts these days.

162
00:13:27.432 --> 00:13:32.729
I'm 68. I'm too old for computers, and
besides, I have a family to provide for.

163
00:13:32.938 --> 00:13:35.816
I love you. And Peter loves you.

164
00:13:36.066 --> 00:13:39.319
You're the most responsible man
I've ever known.

165
00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:43.991
We've been down-and-out before.
But somehow, we survive.

166
00:13:45.117 --> 00:13:49.413
Hi, sweetie. You're just...
Just in time for dinner.

167
00:13:49.621 --> 00:13:52.165
How you doing? How was the field trip?

168
00:13:52.332 --> 00:13:55.169
I don't feel well.
I'm gonna go to sleep.

169
00:13:55.335 --> 00:13:57.838
- You won't have a bite?
- Had a bite.

170
00:13:58.005 --> 00:14:00.424
Did you get some pictures, Peter?

171
00:14:01.258 --> 00:14:04.094
I gotta crash. Everything's fine.

172
00:14:05.512 --> 00:14:07.097
What's that all about?

173
00:14:28.368 --> 00:14:30.579
<i>In this recombination lab...</i>

174
00:14:30.746 --> 00:14:35.375
<i>we use synthesized transfer RNA
to encode an entirely new genome...</i>

175
00:14:35.584 --> 00:14:38.629
<i>combining the genetic
information from all three...</i>

176
00:14:38.837 --> 00:14:43.634
<i>into these 15 genetically
designed super-spiders.</i>

177
00:14:58.106 --> 00:15:02.069
Dr. Osborn, please.
The performance enhancers aren't ready.

178
00:15:02.236 --> 00:15:05.572
The data just doesn't justify
this test.

179
00:15:05.739 --> 00:15:09.409
Now, I'm asking you for the last time.
We can't do this.

180
00:15:09.576 --> 00:15:11.787
Don't be a coward.

181
00:15:12.246 --> 00:15:14.831
Risks are part of laboratory science.

182
00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:18.752
Let me reschedule,
with a medical staff and a volunteer.

183
00:15:18.961 --> 00:15:21.421
- Just give me two weeks.
- Two weeks?

184
00:15:21.588 --> 00:15:26.093
In two weeks? We'll have lost the contract
to Quest and OSCORP will be dead.

185
00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:29.012
Sometimes you gotta
do things yourself.

186
00:15:29.179 --> 00:15:31.849
- Get me the Promachloraperazine.
- For what?

187
00:15:32.015 --> 00:15:35.769
It begins catalyzation when the vapor
hits the bloodstream.

188
00:15:38.689 --> 00:15:40.357
40,000 years of evolution...

189
00:15:40.524 --> 00:15:44.278
and we've barely tapped
the vastness of human potential.

190
00:15:58.125 --> 00:15:59.459
Oh, that's cold.

191
00:16:57.935 --> 00:16:59.186
Norman?

192
00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:04.983
Norman!

193
00:17:15.702 --> 00:17:17.037
Oh, my God.

194
00:17:18.539 --> 00:17:19.957
Oh, my God!

195
00:17:22.626 --> 00:17:24.461
Oh, my God! Norman!

196
00:17:40.853 --> 00:17:42.479
Back to formula?

197
00:18:17.097 --> 00:18:18.599
Weird.

198
00:18:29.526 --> 00:18:30.903
- Peter?
- Yeah?

199
00:18:31.111 --> 00:18:32.863
Are you all right?

200
00:18:34.781 --> 00:18:36.408
I'm fine.

201
00:18:36.992 --> 00:18:40.370
- Any better this morning? Any change?
- Change?

202
00:18:41.371 --> 00:18:43.290
Yep. Big change.

203
00:18:43.457 --> 00:18:47.461
- Well, hurry up. You'll be late.
- Right.

204
00:19:05.854 --> 00:19:07.231
Okay.

205
00:19:11.944 --> 00:19:15.739
- Goodness me!
- Jeez. I thought you were sick.

206
00:19:16.281 --> 00:19:17.616
- I got better.
- See?

207
00:19:17.783 --> 00:19:21.161
- Bye, guys.
- Have you got your lunch money?

208
00:19:21.328 --> 00:19:24.998
Don't forget, we're painting
the kitchen after school.

209
00:19:25.165 --> 00:19:27.960
Sure, Uncle Ben.
Don't start without me.

210
00:19:28.168 --> 00:19:30.254
And don't start up with me.

211
00:19:31.839 --> 00:19:35.509
Teenagers. Raging hormones.
They never change.

212
00:19:36.468 --> 00:19:40.180
You're trash!
You're always gonna be trash!

213
00:19:40.347 --> 00:19:43.934
- I have to go to school.
- Who's stopping you?

214
00:20:01.326 --> 00:20:02.995
Hi, M.J.

215
00:20:03.871 --> 00:20:05.372
Hey, M.J.

216
00:20:05.622 --> 00:20:10.169
I don't know if you realize this, but
we've been neighbors since I was 6.

217
00:20:10.335 --> 00:20:13.672
And I was wondering
if we could get together sometime?

218
00:20:13.881 --> 00:20:15.174
I got the car. Hop in.

219
00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:18.218
Do something fun?
Or, I don't know.

220
00:20:18.427 --> 00:20:22.264
I thought it'd be time
to get to know each other.

221
00:20:22.514 --> 00:20:23.765
Or not.

222
00:20:29.229 --> 00:20:31.940
Sorry, Parker, the bus is full!

223
00:20:33.483 --> 00:20:36.028
- Stop the bus!
- Catch a cab!

224
00:20:36.445 --> 00:20:38.071
Tell him to stop.

225
00:20:38.739 --> 00:20:40.741
- Check him out!
- Dork!

226
00:21:03.222 --> 00:21:04.473
Dad!

227
00:21:04.932 --> 00:21:06.808
Dad, are you all right?

228
00:21:07.643 --> 00:21:08.936
Harry.

229
00:21:12.272 --> 00:21:14.274
What are you doing on the floor?

230
00:21:14.441 --> 00:21:15.776
I don't know.

231
00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:18.946
Have you been there all night?

232
00:21:20.948 --> 00:21:22.199
Last night I was...

233
00:21:24.535 --> 00:21:25.786
What?

234
00:21:27.037 --> 00:21:29.456
- I don't remember.
- Mr. Osborn?

235
00:21:29.665 --> 00:21:31.333
Sir, I asked her to wait.

236
00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:35.838
- My father's not feeling well...
- Mr. Osborn, Dr. Stromm is dead.

237
00:21:36.004 --> 00:21:37.047
What?

238
00:21:37.214 --> 00:21:40.801
They found his body in the lab.
He's been murdered, sir.

239
00:21:40.968 --> 00:21:44.346
- What?
- And the flight suit and the glider...

240
00:21:44.513 --> 00:21:46.515
- What about it?
- Stolen, sir.

241
00:22:11.456 --> 00:22:14.209
Wow! Great reflexes!

242
00:22:15.085 --> 00:22:17.254
- Thanks.
- No problem.

243
00:22:18.338 --> 00:22:22.259
Hey, you have blue eyes.
I didn't notice without your glasses.

244
00:22:23.010 --> 00:22:24.678
You just get contacts?

245
00:22:31.435 --> 00:22:33.604
Well, see you.

246
00:23:15.395 --> 00:23:18.899
- What happened?
- He's freaking weird.

247
00:23:19.358 --> 00:23:20.734
Did you see that?

248
00:23:22.319 --> 00:23:23.987
Parker?

249
00:23:55.853 --> 00:23:58.272
- It's a fight!
- Think you're funny?

250
00:23:58.438 --> 00:24:01.441
- It was an accident.
- So is my breaking your teeth.

251
00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:04.361
- Flash, stop.
- I don't want to fight you.

252
00:24:04.528 --> 00:24:07.948
- I wouldn't want to fight me neither.
- Kick his ass.

253
00:24:26.842 --> 00:24:28.177
Help him, Harry.

254
00:24:33.140 --> 00:24:34.641
How'd he do that?

255
00:24:35.726 --> 00:24:36.977
Which one?

256
00:24:37.144 --> 00:24:38.520
He's all yours, man.

257
00:24:54.036 --> 00:24:55.746
Flash, get up!

258
00:24:57.372 --> 00:25:00.501
Jesus, Parker, you are a freak.

259
00:25:02.419 --> 00:25:03.921
That was amazing.

260
00:25:04.838 --> 00:25:06.840
I'm out of here. Come on.

261
00:26:52.029 --> 00:26:53.071
Go, web!

262
00:26:54.656 --> 00:26:56.283
Fly.

263
00:26:57.868 --> 00:26:59.953
Up, up and away, web.

264
00:27:01.538 --> 00:27:02.956
Shazam!

265
00:27:03.540 --> 00:27:04.791
Go! Go!

266
00:27:05.042 --> 00:27:06.793
Go, web, go!

267
00:27:39.910 --> 00:27:41.662
Tallyho.

268
00:28:25.581 --> 00:28:28.166
- Is she back with the beer yet?
- What?

269
00:28:28.375 --> 00:28:29.626
Bring me some beer.

270
00:28:29.835 --> 00:28:32.379
- Get up off your ass.
- I paid for beer...

271
00:28:32.546 --> 00:28:34.047
- Stop yelling.
- Stop it!

272
00:28:34.214 --> 00:28:36.550
You're as stupid as your mother.

273
00:28:38.468 --> 00:28:41.013
Where's she going?
Where you going?

274
00:28:42.097 --> 00:28:45.434
The dishes aren't done.
Somebody's gotta do dishes.

275
00:28:45.642 --> 00:28:48.937
- Why don't you do them?
- Get in here and do the dishes.

276
00:28:49.146 --> 00:28:53.275
- You do them. They're yours, anyway.
- I'm going out!

277
00:28:53.483 --> 00:28:55.986
- Were you listening to that?
- No.

278
00:28:56.320 --> 00:28:59.573
Well, I heard, but I was
just taking out the trash.

279
00:28:59.740 --> 00:29:02.492
I guess you can always hear us.

280
00:29:02.659 --> 00:29:04.953
Everybody shouts.

281
00:29:05.412 --> 00:29:07.539
Your aunt and uncle don't.

282
00:29:07.706 --> 00:29:10.250
Oh, they can scream
pretty good sometimes.

283
00:29:11.668 --> 00:29:15.881
Listen, M.J., about today
at school with Flash...

284
00:29:16.131 --> 00:29:17.758
You really freaked us out.

285
00:29:17.966 --> 00:29:20.219
I'm sorry. Is he okay?

286
00:29:20.511 --> 00:29:24.473
He's just happy you didn't give him
a black eye for graduation.

287
00:29:27.559 --> 00:29:30.771
So where are you going
after you graduate?

288
00:29:35.526 --> 00:29:37.819
I wanna move into the city.

289
00:29:38.737 --> 00:29:43.534
And hopefully, get a job
as a photographer.

290
00:29:43.700 --> 00:29:46.537
Work my way through college.

291
00:29:47.538 --> 00:29:48.872
What about you?

292
00:29:49.039 --> 00:29:51.041
Headed for the city too.

293
00:29:51.750 --> 00:29:54.002
Can't wait to get out of here.

294
00:29:55.170 --> 00:29:56.672
I wanna...

295
00:29:57.923 --> 00:29:59.424
What?

296
00:30:02.261 --> 00:30:04.513
No, come on. Try me.

297
00:30:05.430 --> 00:30:06.932
I wanna...

298
00:30:08.058 --> 00:30:09.393
act...

299
00:30:10.561 --> 00:30:12.062
on-stage.

300
00:30:12.646 --> 00:30:14.481
Really?

301
00:30:14.857 --> 00:30:17.025
Oh, that's perfect.

302
00:30:17.317 --> 00:30:19.862
You were awesome
in all the school plays.

303
00:30:20.195 --> 00:30:22.030
- Really?
- Yeah.

304
00:30:22.656 --> 00:30:25.659
I cried like a baby
when you played Cinderella.

305
00:30:26.159 --> 00:30:28.370
Peter, that was first grade.

306
00:30:28.871 --> 00:30:30.372
Well...

307
00:30:30.914 --> 00:30:32.416
even so.

308
00:30:33.417 --> 00:30:35.335
Sometimes...

309
00:30:36.170 --> 00:30:37.838
you know people.

310
00:30:39.006 --> 00:30:42.593
You can just see what's coming.

311
00:30:45.679 --> 00:30:48.432
What do you see coming for you?

312
00:30:51.018 --> 00:30:52.686
I don't know.

313
00:30:55.022 --> 00:30:59.693
Whatever it is, it's something
I never felt before.

314
00:31:03.280 --> 00:31:06.200
And what for me?

315
00:31:06.366 --> 00:31:07.701
For you?

316
00:31:09.119 --> 00:31:11.872
You're gonna light up Broadway.

317
00:31:13.373 --> 00:31:14.708
You know...

318
00:31:19.087 --> 00:31:21.715
you're taller than you look.

319
00:31:21.882 --> 00:31:23.425
I hunch.

320
00:31:25.677 --> 00:31:27.179
Don't.

321
00:31:30.724 --> 00:31:34.269
Hey, M.J.! Come take a ride
in my new birthday present.

322
00:31:35.354 --> 00:31:36.647
Come on.

323
00:31:37.731 --> 00:31:39.066
I gotta go.

324
00:31:39.900 --> 00:31:41.068
Bye.

325
00:31:41.735 --> 00:31:44.404
- Oh, my God, it's gorgeous!
- Yeah, right.

326
00:31:44.571 --> 00:31:46.573
- Look at it!
- Hop in.

327
00:31:46.740 --> 00:31:48.992
Oh, my God. What a cool car!

328
00:31:49.243 --> 00:31:50.827
Pretty tight, huh?

329
00:31:51.245 --> 00:31:55.582
Wait till you hear the sound system.
Hey, don't scratch the leather.

330
00:31:57.334 --> 00:31:58.585
Cool car.

331
00:33:31.303 --> 00:33:33.347
What's going on in there?

332
00:33:33.555 --> 00:33:36.183
I'm exercising.
I'm not dressed, Aunt May.

333
00:33:36.350 --> 00:33:40.020
Well, you're acting
so strangely, Peter.

334
00:33:40.312 --> 00:33:42.397
Okay. Thanks.

335
00:34:13.220 --> 00:34:16.557
Something's wrong.
Maybe he's too embarrassed to tell me.

336
00:34:16.723 --> 00:34:19.393
Maybe I'm too embarrassed to ask him.

337
00:34:20.185 --> 00:34:22.229
I just don't know anymore.

338
00:34:22.646 --> 00:34:25.190
I'm going to the library.
See you later.

339
00:34:25.399 --> 00:34:28.777
- Wait. I'll drive you there.
- I'll take the train.

340
00:34:28.944 --> 00:34:32.197
No, I need the exercise.
Go on. Go, go.

341
00:34:43.250 --> 00:34:46.712
- Thanks for the ride, Uncle Ben.
- Wait. We need to talk.

342
00:34:46.879 --> 00:34:51.258
- We can talk later.
- Well, we can talk now. If you let me.

343
00:34:52.134 --> 00:34:54.386
What do we have to talk about?
Why now?

344
00:34:54.553 --> 00:34:58.599
We haven't talked for so long.
May and I don't know who you are.

345
00:34:58.765 --> 00:35:03.770
You shirk your chores. You have all
those weird experiments in your room.

346
00:35:03.937 --> 00:35:08.066
- You start fights at school.
- I told you I didn't start that fight.

347
00:35:08.275 --> 00:35:11.236
- You sure finished it.
- Was I supposed to run away?

348
00:35:11.445 --> 00:35:14.448
No, you're not supposed
to run away, but...

349
00:35:14.615 --> 00:35:19.161
You're changing. I went through
exactly the same thing at your age.

350
00:35:19.369 --> 00:35:21.371
No. Not exactly.

351
00:35:22.748 --> 00:35:25.459
These are the years
when a man changes...

352
00:35:25.626 --> 00:35:29.630
into the man he's gonna become
the rest of his life.

353
00:35:29.796 --> 00:35:32.883
Just be careful who you change into.

354
00:35:34.426 --> 00:35:38.931
This guy, Flash Thompson,
he probably deserved what happened.

355
00:35:39.473 --> 00:35:42.184
But just because you can
beat him up...

356
00:35:42.643 --> 00:35:44.895
doesn't give you the right to.

357
00:35:45.562 --> 00:35:50.817
Remember, with great power
comes great responsibility.

358
00:35:51.401 --> 00:35:56.406
Are you afraid I'll become a criminal?
Quit worrying about me, okay?

359
00:35:56.573 --> 00:35:59.993
Something's different.
I'll figure it out. Stop lecturing.

360
00:36:00.285 --> 00:36:04.498
I don't mean to lecture or preach.
And I know I'm not your father.

361
00:36:04.665 --> 00:36:07.501
Then stop pretending to be!

362
00:36:11.588 --> 00:36:12.840
Right.

363
00:36:15.801 --> 00:36:17.761
I'll pick you up here at 10.

364
00:36:49.001 --> 00:36:54.840
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

365
00:36:59.553 --> 00:37:03.599
- One, two, three. That's it!
- Who's the man?

366
00:37:07.728 --> 00:37:09.938
Ladies and gentlemen...

367
00:37:10.105 --> 00:37:14.651
give it up for Bone Saw McGraw.

368
00:37:17.738 --> 00:37:21.408
For $3000...

369
00:37:21.575 --> 00:37:25.204
is there no one here man enough
to stay in the ring...

370
00:37:25.370 --> 00:37:30.083
for three minutes
with this titan of testosterone?

371
00:37:32.669 --> 00:37:34.755
Who?

372
00:37:35.005 --> 00:37:36.882
I know who.

373
00:37:37.090 --> 00:37:41.887
The Flying Dutchman!

374
00:37:42.221 --> 00:37:43.680
Next.

375
00:37:44.515 --> 00:37:47.809
There's no featherweight
division here. Next.

376
00:37:47.976 --> 00:37:49.811
No, no. Sign me up.

377
00:37:50.229 --> 00:37:53.649
Okay. You understand the NYWL
is not responsible...

378
00:37:53.857 --> 00:37:58.028
for any injury you may and probably
will sustain in said event?

379
00:37:58.237 --> 00:38:01.365
And you're participating
under your own free will?

380
00:38:01.532 --> 00:38:05.577
Down the hall to the ramp.
May God be with you. Next.

381
00:38:08.163 --> 00:38:10.415
Told you! Told you!

382
00:38:10.624 --> 00:38:12.417
Winner!

383
00:38:12.626 --> 00:38:13.836
Next victim!

384
00:38:15.712 --> 00:38:18.590
Are you ready for more?

385
00:38:19.716 --> 00:38:23.303
Bone Saw is ready!

386
00:38:25.722 --> 00:38:30.394
Will the next victim please
enter the arena at this time?

387
00:38:30.602 --> 00:38:35.315
If he can withstand just three minutes
in the cage with Bone Saw McGraw...

388
00:38:35.566 --> 00:38:39.945
the sum of $3000 will be paid to...

389
00:38:40.821 --> 00:38:43.824
- What's your name, kid?
- The Human Spider.

390
00:38:44.408 --> 00:38:46.785
That's it? That's the best you got?

391
00:38:46.952 --> 00:38:49.079
- Yeah.
- Oh, that sucks.

392
00:38:49.246 --> 00:38:53.750
The sum of $3000 will be paid to...

393
00:38:53.917 --> 00:38:57.171
the terrifying, the deadly...

394
00:38:57.421 --> 00:39:00.632
the amazing Spider-Man!

395
00:39:03.010 --> 00:39:05.637
- It's "The Human Spider."
- Get out there.

396
00:39:05.804 --> 00:39:08.849
- No, he got my name wrong.
- Get out there, moron.

397
00:39:11.351 --> 00:39:13.896
Bone Saw will eat you up
and spit you out.

398
00:39:14.146 --> 00:39:16.190
I hope you brought your mommy.

399
00:39:16.356 --> 00:39:20.611
- We'll break you!
- You'll need someone to cry to.

400
00:39:21.153 --> 00:39:26.283
I'm gonna rip all eight of your
feeble legs off one by one.

401
00:39:26.783 --> 00:39:28.827
Oh, my God!

402
00:39:29.036 --> 00:39:30.662
Oh, my legs!

403
00:39:30.829 --> 00:39:33.457
Oh, God. I can't feel my legs.

404
00:39:33.624 --> 00:39:35.626
Kill! Kill! Kill!

405
00:39:43.884 --> 00:39:45.385
Cage! Cage! Cage!

406
00:39:45.552 --> 00:39:46.762
Cage!

407
00:39:56.104 --> 00:39:57.564
Hello? Guys?

408
00:39:58.607 --> 00:40:03.570
Will the guards please lock
the cage doors at this time?

409
00:40:04.279 --> 00:40:08.575
This is some kind of mistake.
I didn't sign up for a cage match!

410
00:40:09.743 --> 00:40:12.246
Unlock the thing! Take the chain off!

411
00:40:12.454 --> 00:40:14.248
Hey, freak show!

412
00:40:14.456 --> 00:40:17.084
You're going nowhere.

413
00:40:17.251 --> 00:40:19.628
I got you for three minutes.

414
00:40:19.795 --> 00:40:22.089
Three minutes of playtime.

415
00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:32.182
- What are you doing up there?
- Staying away from you.

416
00:40:32.391 --> 00:40:36.436
That's a cute outfit.
Did your husband give it to you?

417
00:40:42.109 --> 00:40:43.652
Finish him off!

418
00:40:50.826 --> 00:40:52.369
Smash him!

419
00:40:59.543 --> 00:41:01.295
- Hit him!
- Harder!

420
00:41:03.297 --> 00:41:05.632
Kick his spider ass!

421
00:41:07.634 --> 00:41:08.802
Hit him!

422
00:41:22.232 --> 00:41:24.026
One, two, three!

423
00:41:24.234 --> 00:41:27.029
That's it! That's it!
Winner!

424
00:41:27.196 --> 00:41:32.284
Ladies and gentlemen, give it up
for the new champion, Spider-Man!

425
00:41:49.676 --> 00:41:51.345
Now get out of here.

426
00:41:52.971 --> 00:41:55.807
A hundred bucks? The ad said 3000.

427
00:41:56.016 --> 00:41:58.393
Well, check it again, webhead.

428
00:41:58.560 --> 00:42:02.439
It said three grand for three minutes.
You pinned him in two.

429
00:42:02.648 --> 00:42:06.026
For that, I give you 100.
You're lucky to get that.

430
00:42:06.193 --> 00:42:07.569
I need that money.

431
00:42:08.028 --> 00:42:11.114
I missed the part
where that's my problem.

432
00:42:19.206 --> 00:42:22.543
- Hey, what the hell...?
- Put the money in the bag.

433
00:42:24.378 --> 00:42:25.712
Hurry up!

434
00:42:32.052 --> 00:42:34.137
Hey! He stole the gate!

435
00:42:34.304 --> 00:42:36.265
Stop that guy!

436
00:42:36.557 --> 00:42:39.101
Stop him! He's got my money!

437
00:42:39.309 --> 00:42:40.561
Thanks.

438
00:42:41.812 --> 00:42:44.189
What's wrong with you?
You let him go!

439
00:42:44.356 --> 00:42:46.608
Cut him off and call the cops!

440
00:42:46.775 --> 00:42:50.821
You could've taken that guy apart.
Now he'll get away.

441
00:42:50.988 --> 00:42:54.366
I missed the part
where that's my problem.

442
00:43:12.759 --> 00:43:15.679
- You gotta get back.
- I can't see. What happened?

443
00:43:16.930 --> 00:43:18.307
Old dude, man.

444
00:43:18.515 --> 00:43:22.686
Come on, folks. Keep moving, please.
Keep moving. Let's go!

445
00:43:22.853 --> 00:43:25.689
- What happened?
- Someone got hurt.

446
00:43:28.066 --> 00:43:31.278
- Excuse me. Excuse me. Excuse me.
- Stay back.

447
00:43:31.778 --> 00:43:33.614
- Stay back!
- That's my uncle!

448
00:43:35.782 --> 00:43:38.410
- What happened?
- Carjacker. He's been shot.

449
00:43:38.535 --> 00:43:42.080
We just called the paramedics.
They're on their way.

450
00:43:42.289 --> 00:43:43.665
Uncle Ben?

451
00:43:44.583 --> 00:43:46.084
Uncle Ben.

452
00:43:49.838 --> 00:43:51.173
Uncle Ben?

453
00:43:54.801 --> 00:43:56.303
Peter.

454
00:43:57.179 --> 00:43:58.972
I'm here, Uncle Ben.

455
00:44:04.603 --> 00:44:05.812
Peter.

456
00:44:27.793 --> 00:44:30.838
They got the shooter.
He's headed south on Fifth.

457
00:44:31.046 --> 00:44:35.759
We got three cars in pursuit.
All right, folks. Come on, move back.

458
00:47:12.875 --> 00:47:14.793
Get a unit to the rear!

459
00:47:17.838 --> 00:47:19.381
I got the back!

460
00:47:32.311 --> 00:47:33.645
Who's there?

461
00:47:59.922 --> 00:48:03.050
Don't hurt me. Give me a chance.
Give me a chance!

462
00:48:03.217 --> 00:48:07.721
What about my uncle?
Did you give him a chance? Did you?

463
00:48:07.888 --> 00:48:09.389
Answer me!

464
00:48:12.726 --> 00:48:14.061
<i>Stop that guy!</i>

465
00:48:19.525 --> 00:48:21.235
<i>Thanks.</i>

466
00:48:31.119 --> 00:48:32.246
See you.

467
00:48:53.934 --> 00:48:57.396
<i>Freeze! We've got the place
completely surrounded.</i>

468
00:49:39.897 --> 00:49:42.566
Oh, no. My God.

469
00:49:44.443 --> 00:49:48.155
Oh, no.
Oh, my God. No!

470
00:49:56.496 --> 00:49:59.458
- Good evening.
- General. Good to see you.

471
00:50:00.250 --> 00:50:03.128
Our exoskeleton's got
real firepower, general.

472
00:50:03.295 --> 00:50:08.717
Well, if it does what you say it can,
I'll sign that contract tomorrow.

473
00:50:09.426 --> 00:50:12.971
- He's clear! Go!
- You're confident about this test?

474
00:50:13.138 --> 00:50:15.432
Absolutely. Curtis is our top pilot.

475
00:50:16.183 --> 00:50:18.936
Now, what about
your commitment to OSCORP?

476
00:50:19.102 --> 00:50:23.023
Nothing would please me more
than to put Osborn out of business.

477
00:50:25.359 --> 00:50:28.403
Preflight complete. Mark.

478
00:50:32.533 --> 00:50:35.160
<i>An unidentified object
is closing fast.</i>

479
00:50:35.327 --> 00:50:36.411
What's that?

480
00:50:36.578 --> 00:50:38.080
<i>Can you see anything?</i>

481
00:50:38.539 --> 00:50:39.915
Oh, my God!

482
00:50:50.217 --> 00:50:53.053
- Say "chess."
- Chess!

483
00:50:53.554 --> 00:50:55.430
Peter!

484
00:50:55.639 --> 00:51:00.185
Darling, I'm so proud of you.
You looked so handsome up there.

485
00:51:00.352 --> 00:51:03.856
Dad got the place in New York,
so we're all set for fall.

486
00:51:04.022 --> 00:51:05.566
- Great!
- You made it.

487
00:51:08.318 --> 00:51:11.655
It's not the first time
I've been proven wrong.

488
00:51:13.073 --> 00:51:15.242
- Congratulations.
- Thanks, Dad.

489
00:51:15.659 --> 00:51:18.245
Peter, the science award.
That's terrific.

490
00:51:18.662 --> 00:51:19.955
Yeah.

491
00:51:22.916 --> 00:51:26.295
I know this has been
a difficult time for you...

492
00:51:26.461 --> 00:51:29.715
but I want you to try
to enjoy this day.

493
00:51:29.923 --> 00:51:31.466
Commencement:

494
00:51:31.633 --> 00:51:35.762
The end of one thing,
the start of something new.

495
00:51:37.598 --> 00:51:41.268
I don't want to be with you anymore.
Here's your ring.

496
00:51:42.144 --> 00:51:44.021
You know what? Whatever.

497
00:51:44.563 --> 00:51:46.023
Your loss.

498
00:51:46.732 --> 00:51:50.277
You're like a brother to Harry.
That makes you family.

499
00:51:50.444 --> 00:51:54.281
And if you ever need anything,
give me a call.

500
00:52:08.170 --> 00:52:10.422
Can I fix you something?

501
00:52:10.589 --> 00:52:12.090
No, thanks.

502
00:52:56.844 --> 00:52:59.054
I missed him a lot today.

503
00:53:01.640 --> 00:53:03.141
I know.

504
00:53:04.893 --> 00:53:06.728
I miss him too.

505
00:53:08.480 --> 00:53:10.816
But he was there.

506
00:53:13.986 --> 00:53:19.199
I can't help thinking about
the last thing I said to him.

507
00:53:19.491 --> 00:53:24.413
He tried to tell me something important,
and I threw it in his face.

508
00:53:26.164 --> 00:53:28.250
You loved him...

509
00:53:29.918 --> 00:53:32.171
and he loved you.

510
00:53:33.046 --> 00:53:36.717
He never doubted
the man you'd grow into.

511
00:53:36.884 --> 00:53:40.345
How you were meant for great things.

512
00:53:40.888 --> 00:53:43.223
You won't disappoint him.

513
00:54:16.757 --> 00:54:20.928
<i>With great power
comes great responsibility.</i>

514
00:54:21.094 --> 00:54:24.306
<i>Remember that, Pete. Remember that.</i>

515
00:54:34.316 --> 00:54:35.567
Hurry up!

516
00:54:47.955 --> 00:54:51.708
He's not a man. My brother saw him
build a nest in Lincoln Center.

517
00:54:51.875 --> 00:54:55.087
I think he's human, a man.
Could be a woman.

518
00:54:59.174 --> 00:55:01.927
Bobby. Get a load of this!

519
00:55:05.097 --> 00:55:09.351
He throws up his hands,
ropes come out, and he climbs up them.

520
00:55:09.643 --> 00:55:13.772
I see the web, his signature,
and I know Spider-Man was here.

521
00:55:13.939 --> 00:55:16.567
The guy protects us,
protects the people.

522
00:55:16.733 --> 00:55:19.486
Some kind of freakyloo or something.

523
00:55:19.653 --> 00:55:21.697
He stinks and I don't like him.

524
00:55:22.406 --> 00:55:23.991
Don't move, lady!

525
00:55:32.082 --> 00:55:34.835
Guy with eight hands. Sounds hot.

526
00:55:35.043 --> 00:55:37.171
Those tights and that tight little...

527
00:55:37.337 --> 00:55:40.674
<i>Dresses like a spider
He looks like a bug.</i>

528
00:55:40.883 --> 00:55:44.636
<i>But we should all just give him
One big hug.</i>

529
00:55:44.845 --> 00:55:49.433
<i>Look out
Here comes the Spider-Man.</i>

530
00:55:53.103 --> 00:55:56.857
"Who is Spider-Man?"
He's a criminal, that's who he is.

531
00:55:57.024 --> 00:56:01.045
A vigilante, a public menace.
Why's he on my front page?

532
00:56:01.069 --> 00:56:02.529
<i>Mr. Jameson, your wife needs...</i>

533
00:56:03.530 --> 00:56:06.700
- There's a page six problem.
- We have a page one problem.

534
00:56:06.867 --> 00:56:08.410
- Well?
- He's news.

535
00:56:08.619 --> 00:56:11.121
- The clients can't wait.
- They're about to.

536
00:56:11.288 --> 00:56:15.292
- He pulled six people off a subway.
- From a wreck he probably caused.

537
00:56:15.459 --> 00:56:19.630
Something goes wrong and he's there.
Look! He's fleeing the scene.

538
00:56:19.796 --> 00:56:23.759
He's probably going to save
somebody else. He's a hero!

539
00:56:23.926 --> 00:56:26.720
Then why the mask?
What's he got to hide?

540
00:56:26.887 --> 00:56:29.932
She needs to know
if you want chintz or chenille.

541
00:56:30.098 --> 00:56:32.559
- Whichever's cheaper.
- It's like this:

542
00:56:32.726 --> 00:56:36.563
We double-booked page six.
Macy's and Conway's both have...

543
00:56:36.730 --> 00:56:39.900
- We sold out four printings.
- Sold out?

544
00:56:40.067 --> 00:56:41.276
Every copy.

545
00:56:42.069 --> 00:56:45.656
Tomorrow, Spider-Man, page one.
Move Conway to page seven.

546
00:56:45.822 --> 00:56:48.742
- That's a problem.
- Then make it page eight.

547
00:56:48.909 --> 00:56:50.577
- That can't be done.
- Get out!

548
00:56:50.744 --> 00:56:55.624
We can't get a decent picture. Eddie's
on it, but we can barely see him.

549
00:56:55.791 --> 00:56:57.918
Aw, what is he, shy?

550
00:56:58.085 --> 00:57:02.089
If we can get Julia Roberts
in a thong, we can get this weirdo.

551
00:57:02.256 --> 00:57:05.676
On the front page:
"Cash for a Spider-Man picture."

552
00:57:05.843 --> 00:57:09.304
He doesn't want to be famous?
I'll make him infamous!

553
00:57:21.775 --> 00:57:23.193
Buzz off.

554
00:57:23.902 --> 00:57:26.864
- M.J., it's me, Peter.
- Hi!

555
00:57:28.574 --> 00:57:33.453
- What are you doing around here?
- Begging for a job. How about you?

556
00:57:33.954 --> 00:57:37.666
- I'm headed to an audition.
- An audition? So you're acting?

557
00:57:37.833 --> 00:57:38.876
Yeah.

558
00:57:39.084 --> 00:57:42.963
I work steady.
In fact, I just got off a job.

559
00:57:43.130 --> 00:57:44.298
That's great.

560
00:57:44.882 --> 00:57:48.093
- You're doing it. Living your dream.
- Glamour girl!

561
00:57:48.260 --> 00:57:49.887
Your drawer was short $6!

562
00:57:50.053 --> 00:57:52.681
Next time, I'll take it
from your check.

563
00:57:53.765 --> 00:57:57.561
Excuse me, Miss Watson?
I'm talking to you! Hey!

564
00:57:57.769 --> 00:58:00.063
Yes, Enrique! Okay? I get you.

565
00:58:00.230 --> 00:58:04.359
It better not happen no more.
Don't roll your eyes at me.

566
00:58:11.325 --> 00:58:13.035
Some dream, huh?

567
00:58:13.911 --> 00:58:16.538
It's nothing to be
embarrassed about.

568
00:58:16.705 --> 00:58:19.499
- Don't tell Harry.
- Don't tell Harry?

569
00:58:19.917 --> 00:58:24.505
Don't you guys live together?
We're going out. Didn't he tell you?

570
00:58:24.922 --> 00:58:26.507
Oh, yeah. Right.

571
00:58:26.757 --> 00:58:29.843
I think he'd hate the idea
of my waiting tables.

572
00:58:30.010 --> 00:58:34.431
- He'd think it was low or something.
- It's not low. You have a job.

573
00:58:34.765 --> 00:58:39.102
You know, Harry doesn't live on
a little place I like to call Earth.

574
00:58:40.604 --> 00:58:42.523
No, I guess not.

575
00:58:47.528 --> 00:58:49.112
Thanks, Pete.

576
00:58:50.531 --> 00:58:52.449
We should catch up sometime.

577
00:58:56.662 --> 00:58:59.206
Let's get some lunch some evening.

578
00:59:00.457 --> 00:59:04.962
I'll come by and have some of your
Moondance coffee some day.

579
00:59:05.170 --> 00:59:07.881
- And I won't tell Harry.
- Don't tell Harry.

580
00:59:08.048 --> 00:59:09.299
I won't.

581
00:59:11.468 --> 00:59:13.220
I won't tell Harry.

582
00:59:24.523 --> 00:59:26.984
Timing's perfect. Hey.

583
00:59:27.192 --> 00:59:30.487
Five new contracts. It'll be great.

584
00:59:32.614 --> 00:59:35.325
Norman's making his weekly inspection.

585
00:59:36.118 --> 00:59:38.370
Spent half of it on the phone.

586
00:59:38.954 --> 00:59:43.667
Look, man, I'm glad you're here.
I need your help. I'm really lost here.

587
00:59:44.501 --> 00:59:45.794
Are you all right?

588
00:59:47.129 --> 00:59:51.675
You look like you just got
second place in the science fair.

589
00:59:52.968 --> 00:59:55.929
I was late for work
and Dr. Connors fired me.

590
00:59:56.096 --> 00:59:57.639
You were late again?

591
00:59:58.265 --> 01:00:02.227
I don't get it.
Where do you go all the time?

592
01:00:02.394 --> 01:00:03.645
Around.

593
01:00:03.812 --> 01:00:05.522
Peter Parker.

594
01:00:05.856 --> 01:00:08.358
- Maybe you'll tell me who she is.
- Who?

595
01:00:08.525 --> 01:00:11.612
- This mystery girl Harry's been dating.
- Dad.

596
01:00:11.987 --> 01:00:13.655
When do I get to meet her?

597
01:00:13.822 --> 01:00:17.117
Well, sorry.
Harry hasn't mentioned her.

598
01:00:19.995 --> 01:00:23.248
Pete, you're probably looking
for a job now, right?

599
01:00:23.457 --> 01:00:26.293
Dad, maybe you can help him out.

600
01:00:26.460 --> 01:00:30.797
- I appreciate it, but I'll be fine.
- I'll make a few calls.

601
01:00:30.964 --> 01:00:35.260
I couldn't accept it. I like to earn
what I get. I'll find work.

602
01:00:35.469 --> 01:00:37.095
I respect that.

603
01:00:37.804 --> 01:00:39.932
You want to make it on your own.

604
01:00:40.599 --> 01:00:41.934
That's great.

605
01:00:42.809 --> 01:00:45.145
What other skills do you have?

606
01:00:45.354 --> 01:00:47.481
I was thinking about photography.

607
01:00:50.442 --> 01:00:51.693
Hello.

608
01:00:53.612 --> 01:00:55.906
Let's go! Move it!

609
01:00:57.074 --> 01:00:58.742
Watch the street!

610
01:01:14.174 --> 01:01:15.551
Cheese!

611
01:01:24.476 --> 01:01:25.769
They're crap.

612
01:01:25.978 --> 01:01:28.939
Crap, crap. Megacrap.

613
01:01:29.147 --> 01:01:32.317
- I'll give you $200.
- That seems a little low.

614
01:01:32.526 --> 01:01:34.278
Take them somewhere else.

615
01:01:34.695 --> 01:01:38.782
- <i>Your wife says the tile's out of stock.
- We'll put a rug there.</i>

616
01:01:39.157 --> 01:01:41.118
Sit down. Give me that.

617
01:01:42.703 --> 01:01:45.247
Give you 300.
That's the standard fee.

618
01:01:45.414 --> 01:01:47.749
- Scrap page one. Run that.
- Headline?

619
01:01:48.041 --> 01:01:51.253
"Spider-Man, Hero or Menace?
Exclusive Photos."

620
01:01:51.420 --> 01:01:54.548
- Menace? He was protecting...
- You take the photos...

621
01:01:54.756 --> 01:01:57.426
I'll make up the headlines. Okay?

622
01:01:57.593 --> 01:01:59.595
- Yes, sir.
- Goody.

623
01:02:00.053 --> 01:02:03.557
Give this to the girl up front.
She'll see you get paid.

624
01:02:04.016 --> 01:02:06.810
- I'd like a job, sir.
- No jobs. Freelance.

625
01:02:07.019 --> 01:02:08.645
Best thing for you.

626
01:02:08.854 --> 01:02:13.150
You bring me more shots of that clown,
maybe I'll buy them.

627
01:02:13.358 --> 01:02:16.320
But I never said you have a job. Meat.

628
01:02:16.486 --> 01:02:20.782
I'll send you a box of Christmas
meat. Bring me more photos.

629
01:02:22.367 --> 01:02:23.577
- Hi.
- Hi.

630
01:02:23.785 --> 01:02:27.206
Mr. Jameson told me
to give that to you.

631
01:02:28.290 --> 01:02:31.418
- <i>Welcome to the Daily Bugle.
- Thank you.</i>

632
01:02:31.960 --> 01:02:33.337
I'm Peter Parker.

633
01:02:35.839 --> 01:02:38.008
I'm a photographer.

634
01:02:38.800 --> 01:02:41.345
Yes. I can see that.

635
01:02:49.061 --> 01:02:50.896
As of today...

636
01:02:51.063 --> 01:02:55.067
OSCORP Industries has surpassed
Quest Aerospace...

637
01:02:55.317 --> 01:02:59.738
as the principal supplier
to the United States military.

638
01:02:59.905 --> 01:03:02.741
In short, ladies and gentlemen
of the board...

639
01:03:02.908 --> 01:03:06.078
costs are down, revenues are up...

640
01:03:06.328 --> 01:03:09.164
and our stock
has never been higher.

641
01:03:09.331 --> 01:03:13.752
Wonderful news, Norman.
That's why we're selling the company.

642
01:03:14.586 --> 01:03:15.838
What?

643
01:03:16.046 --> 01:03:21.176
Quest is recapitalizing in the wake
of the bombing. Expanding.

644
01:03:21.426 --> 01:03:24.179
They made a tender offer
we can't ignore.

645
01:03:24.346 --> 01:03:25.514
Why wasn't I told?

646
01:03:25.681 --> 01:03:29.768
They don't want a power struggle
with entrenched management.

647
01:03:30.060 --> 01:03:32.354
The deal is off if you come with it.

648
01:03:32.521 --> 01:03:35.941
The board expects your resignation
in 30 days.

649
01:03:36.149 --> 01:03:38.110
You can't do this to me.

650
01:03:41.280 --> 01:03:43.574
I started this company.

651
01:03:44.616 --> 01:03:47.035
You know how much I sacrificed?!

652
01:03:50.873 --> 01:03:56.336
- Oh, Max. Please.
- Norman, the board is unanimous.

653
01:03:56.879 --> 01:04:00.883
We're announcing the sale
after the World Unity Festival.

654
01:04:01.049 --> 01:04:02.551
I'm sorry.

655
01:04:03.552 --> 01:04:05.679
You're out, Norman.

656
01:04:15.564 --> 01:04:17.065
Am I?

657
01:04:24.031 --> 01:04:27.784
<i>Let's hear it for Macy Gray.</i>

658
01:05:04.196 --> 01:05:07.741
M.J., why didn't you wear
the black dress?

659
01:05:08.784 --> 01:05:12.454
Just, I wanted to impress my father.
He loves black.

660
01:05:12.621 --> 01:05:17.167
Well, maybe he'll be impressed
no matter what. You think I'm pretty.

661
01:05:17.709 --> 01:05:20.087
I think you're beautiful.

662
01:05:32.891 --> 01:05:36.144
I forgot my drink inside.

663
01:05:46.363 --> 01:05:48.490
- Oh, hi, Mr. Fargas.
- Oh, Harry.

664
01:05:49.575 --> 01:05:54.746
- Have you seen my father?
- Well, I'm not sure if he's coming.

665
01:06:06.758 --> 01:06:09.261
- What is that?
- Must be new this year.

666
01:06:14.141 --> 01:06:15.434
What is that?

667
01:06:15.601 --> 01:06:17.519
That's our glider!

668
01:06:27.905 --> 01:06:29.364
What the hell was that?

669
01:06:57.768 --> 01:06:59.186
Code three!

670
01:07:15.202 --> 01:07:17.371
- Oh, my God! Harry!
- M.J.!

671
01:07:23.335 --> 01:07:26.797
Harry! Help me! Harry!

672
01:07:32.761 --> 01:07:34.513
Out, am I?

673
01:07:39.059 --> 01:07:42.271
- Mary Jane!
- Harry!

674
01:07:44.273 --> 01:07:46.149
Hello, my dear.

675
01:07:47.150 --> 01:07:48.986
It's Spider-Man!

676
01:08:00.497 --> 01:08:02.457
- Come on. Move, kid.
- Billy!

677
01:08:05.961 --> 01:08:08.297
Somebody help him!

678
01:08:08.505 --> 01:08:10.549
No!

679
01:08:11.550 --> 01:08:13.093
Mommy!

680
01:08:15.095 --> 01:08:17.055
- Hold it!
- I surrender.

681
01:08:17.639 --> 01:08:20.142
- Oh, boy.
- Hold it right there!

682
01:08:25.939 --> 01:08:27.191
Impressive.

683
01:08:51.465 --> 01:08:54.927
- Mary Jane!
- Help! Someone please help me!

684
01:09:20.285 --> 01:09:21.328
Hold on!

685
01:09:22.955 --> 01:09:23.997
Watch out!

686
01:09:33.131 --> 01:09:36.927
We'll meet again, Spider-Man!

687
01:10:22.431 --> 01:10:25.100
Well, beats taking the subway.

688
01:10:25.309 --> 01:10:28.562
Don't mind us.
She just needs to use the elevator.

689
01:10:28.729 --> 01:10:29.855
Wait.

690
01:10:30.022 --> 01:10:31.273
Who are you?

691
01:10:31.440 --> 01:10:34.026
- You know who I am.
- I do?

692
01:10:34.234 --> 01:10:36.862
Your friendly neighborhood Spider-Man.

693
01:10:48.582 --> 01:10:52.461
Incredible?
What do you mean he's incredible?

694
01:10:53.629 --> 01:10:57.299
No. All right, wait.
Stay there. I'll come over.

695
01:10:57.966 --> 01:10:59.635
No, I'm gonna come...

696
01:10:59.968 --> 01:11:03.388
All right. Fine.
Will you call me in the morning?

697
01:11:03.597 --> 01:11:06.558
And we'll go and have breakfast and...

698
01:11:06.725 --> 01:11:09.019
I want to buy you something.

699
01:11:09.186 --> 01:11:12.523
Because I want to.
It'll make you feel better.

700
01:11:13.565 --> 01:11:17.236
Okay. And what do you mean,
incredible?

701
01:11:20.072 --> 01:11:22.449
All right. I'm sorry. Sleep tight.

702
01:11:22.616 --> 01:11:24.368
Don't let the bedbugs...

703
01:11:30.040 --> 01:11:33.085
She's all right.
She's just a little rattled.

704
01:11:34.795 --> 01:11:38.423
Look, Pete, I should have
told you about us.

705
01:11:39.758 --> 01:11:42.427
But you should know
I'm crazy about her.

706
01:11:42.594 --> 01:11:45.639
It's just, you know,
you never made a move.

707
01:11:46.723 --> 01:11:48.225
You're right.

708
01:11:49.142 --> 01:11:50.644
I didn't.

709
01:11:54.648 --> 01:11:57.067
I'm gonna get some rest.

710
01:11:58.318 --> 01:12:00.571
I'm gonna stay up for a while.

711
01:12:01.655 --> 01:12:03.407
What was that thing?

712
01:12:03.991 --> 01:12:05.325
I don't know.

713
01:12:06.743 --> 01:12:10.122
Whatever it is,
somebody has to stop it.

714
01:12:26.013 --> 01:12:27.180
Somebody there?

715
01:12:27.181 --> 01:12:29.975
<i>Somebody.</i>

716
01:12:31.310 --> 01:12:32.853
Who said that?

717
01:12:33.520 --> 01:12:36.857
<i>Don't play the innocent with me.</i>

718
01:12:39.318 --> 01:12:41.987
<i>You've known all along.</i>

719
01:12:45.991 --> 01:12:47.367
Where are you?

720
01:12:47.534 --> 01:12:51.580
<i>Follow the cold shiver
running down your spine.</i>

721
01:12:58.462 --> 01:13:00.297
<i>I'm right here.</i>

722
01:13:02.049 --> 01:13:04.051
I don't understand.

723
01:13:05.052 --> 01:13:08.222
Did you think it was coincidence?

724
01:13:08.472 --> 01:13:12.017
So many good things,
all happening for you.

725
01:13:12.184 --> 01:13:15.854
All for you. Norman.

726
01:13:18.398 --> 01:13:19.816
What do you want?

727
01:13:20.359 --> 01:13:22.402
To say what you won't.

728
01:13:22.694 --> 01:13:25.239
To do what you can't.

729
01:13:25.405 --> 01:13:29.993
To remove those in your way.

730
01:13:33.956 --> 01:13:35.916
The board members.

731
01:13:37.209 --> 01:13:38.585
You killed them.

732
01:13:38.752 --> 01:13:40.295
We killed them.

733
01:13:40.629 --> 01:13:41.672
We?

734
01:13:41.880 --> 01:13:43.423
Remember?

735
01:13:43.590 --> 01:13:46.260
Your little accident
in the laboratory.

736
01:13:48.136 --> 01:13:49.930
The performance enhancers.

737
01:13:50.097 --> 01:13:55.394
Bingo. Me!
Your greatest creation.

738
01:13:55.602 --> 01:13:59.398
Bringing you
what you've always wanted:

739
01:13:59.565 --> 01:14:02.442
Power beyond your wildest dreams.

740
01:14:02.609 --> 01:14:05.112
And it's only the beginning.

741
01:14:06.613 --> 01:14:10.951
There's only one who can stop us.

742
01:14:11.743 --> 01:14:15.122
Or imagine if he joined us.

743
01:14:19.918 --> 01:14:23.130
Spider-Man. And the Green Goblin.

744
01:14:23.380 --> 01:14:26.633
The Green Goblin. You like that?
Made it up myself.

745
01:14:26.800 --> 01:14:29.803
- These weirdos all got to have a name.
- Mr. Jameson...

746
01:14:29.970 --> 01:14:31.638
- Hoffman!
- Yeah?

747
01:14:32.848 --> 01:14:36.602
Copyright "Green Goblin."
I want a quarter every time it's said.

748
01:14:36.810 --> 01:14:39.104
How about "Green Meanie"?

749
01:14:39.271 --> 01:14:42.149
Spider-Man wasn't attacking.
That's slander.

750
01:14:42.316 --> 01:14:44.651
It is not. I resent that.

751
01:14:44.902 --> 01:14:47.654
Slander is spoken.
In print, it's libel.

752
01:14:47.821 --> 01:14:49.489
You don't trust anybody.

753
01:14:49.948 --> 01:14:51.700
I trust my barber.

754
01:14:52.534 --> 01:14:54.036
Are you his lawyer?

755
01:14:54.244 --> 01:14:58.999
Let him sue. Get rich like a normal
person. That's what made this country...

756
01:15:06.507 --> 01:15:09.635
Jameson, you slime.

757
01:15:09.843 --> 01:15:13.138
Who takes the pictures of Spider-Man?

758
01:15:13.347 --> 01:15:16.266
- I don't know. His stuff comes by mail.
- Liar!

759
01:15:16.433 --> 01:15:19.436
- I swear.
- He's the one who can bring me to him.

760
01:15:19.603 --> 01:15:22.523
- I don't know who he is.
- You are useless.

761
01:15:22.731 --> 01:15:24.983
Set him down, tough guy.

762
01:15:25.234 --> 01:15:29.821
- Speak of the devil.
- I knew you two were in this together!

763
01:15:30.030 --> 01:15:32.616
Kiddo, let Mom and Dad
talk for a minute.

764
01:15:32.824 --> 01:15:35.285
Sleep...

765
01:15:49.758 --> 01:15:53.762
Wake up, little spider. Wake up.

766
01:15:53.929 --> 01:15:58.350
No, you're not dead yet.

767
01:15:58.559 --> 01:16:00.727
Just paralyzed...

768
01:16:00.894 --> 01:16:02.855
temporarily.

769
01:16:03.856 --> 01:16:06.942
You're an amazing creature,
Spider-Man.

770
01:16:07.150 --> 01:16:09.820
You and I are not so different.

771
01:16:10.529 --> 01:16:13.866
I'm not like you. You're a murderer.

772
01:16:14.074 --> 01:16:16.952
Well, to each his own.

773
01:16:17.119 --> 01:16:20.080
I chose my path,
you chose the way of the hero.

774
01:16:20.747 --> 01:16:25.377
And they found you amusing
for a while, the people of this city.

775
01:16:25.586 --> 01:16:28.839
But the one thing they love
more than a hero...

776
01:16:29.047 --> 01:16:32.634
is to see a hero fail,
fall, die trying.

777
01:16:32.801 --> 01:16:37.347
In spite of everything you've done for
them, eventually, they will hate you.

778
01:16:37.556 --> 01:16:38.599
Why bother?

779
01:16:38.807 --> 01:16:43.520
- Because it's right.
- Here's the real truth.

780
01:16:43.937 --> 01:16:46.940
There are eight million people
in this city.

781
01:16:47.149 --> 01:16:51.445
And those teeming masses exist
for the sole purpose...

782
01:16:51.653 --> 01:16:55.616
of lifting the few exceptional
people onto their shoulders.

783
01:16:55.782 --> 01:16:57.201
You, me...

784
01:16:57.784 --> 01:16:59.703
we're exceptional.

785
01:16:59.953 --> 01:17:04.625
I could squash you like a bug
right now.

786
01:17:04.833 --> 01:17:08.504
But I'm offering you a choice.
Join me.

787
01:17:08.670 --> 01:17:12.257
Imagine what we could
accomplish together.

788
01:17:12.466 --> 01:17:15.219
What we could create.

789
01:17:15.802 --> 01:17:17.804
Or we could destroy.

790
01:17:17.971 --> 01:17:21.934
Cause the deaths of countless
innocents in selfish battle...

791
01:17:22.142 --> 01:17:27.022
again and again and again until
we're both dead. Is that what you want?

792
01:17:29.024 --> 01:17:31.902
Think about it, hero.

793
01:17:43.872 --> 01:17:49.211
<i>In spite of everything you've done for
them, eventually, they will hate you.</i>

794
01:17:59.555 --> 01:18:01.014
It's me again.

795
01:18:01.390 --> 01:18:02.808
How was your audition?

796
01:18:03.016 --> 01:18:06.019
- How'd you know?
- The hot line. Your mom...

797
01:18:06.186 --> 01:18:08.146
told my aunt, told me.

798
01:18:08.605 --> 01:18:09.940
So you just came by?

799
01:18:10.148 --> 01:18:13.777
I was in the neighborhood.
Needed to see a friendly face.

800
01:18:13.944 --> 01:18:18.532
I took two buses and a cab
to get in the neighborhood, but...

801
01:18:18.782 --> 01:18:20.284
So how'd it go?

802
01:18:22.452 --> 01:18:25.038
They said I needed acting lessons.

803
01:18:25.205 --> 01:18:28.959
A soap opera told me
I needed acting lessons.

804
01:18:29.126 --> 01:18:34.464
Let me buy you a cheeseburger.
The sky's the limit, up to $7.84.

805
01:18:35.799 --> 01:18:37.885
I'd like a cheeseburger.

806
01:18:38.343 --> 01:18:41.805
Oh, but I'm going out to dinner
with Harry.

807
01:18:42.222 --> 01:18:43.640
Come with us.

808
01:18:43.807 --> 01:18:46.560
No, thanks. How's it going with?

809
01:18:48.478 --> 01:18:50.981
Never mind.
That's none of my business.

810
01:18:51.481 --> 01:18:52.983
It's not?

811
01:18:54.401 --> 01:18:56.069
Why so interested?

812
01:18:56.737 --> 01:18:58.238
I'm not.

813
01:18:58.488 --> 01:18:59.865
You're not?

814
01:19:01.491 --> 01:19:04.244
- Well, why would I be?
- I don't know.

815
01:19:04.494 --> 01:19:06.288
Why would you be?

816
01:19:08.165 --> 01:19:10.501
I, that's a...

817
01:19:10.709 --> 01:19:12.211
I don't know.

818
01:19:14.421 --> 01:19:17.257
Sorry you won't come with us.

819
01:19:19.718 --> 01:19:21.678
I'd better run, tiger.

820
01:19:30.395 --> 01:19:32.397
Hey, check it out, man.

821
01:19:32.564 --> 01:19:34.233
Come on, man.

822
01:19:37.778 --> 01:19:41.031
Hey, where you going, baby?
Come on!

823
01:19:58.924 --> 01:20:00.384
Get off me!

824
01:20:33.667 --> 01:20:35.169
Wait!

825
01:20:40.007 --> 01:20:42.384
You have a knack
for getting in trouble.

826
01:20:42.551 --> 01:20:46.930
You have a knack for saving my life.
I think I have a superhero stalker.

827
01:20:47.139 --> 01:20:49.016
I was in the neighborhood.

828
01:20:50.893 --> 01:20:53.520
You are amazing.

829
01:20:54.479 --> 01:20:57.191
Some people don't think so.

830
01:20:58.275 --> 01:21:01.278
- But you are.
- Nice to have a fan.

831
01:21:02.029 --> 01:21:05.240
Do I get to say thank you this time?

832
01:21:06.116 --> 01:21:07.618
Wait.

833
01:22:16.603 --> 01:22:18.730
Let me in! My baby's in there!

834
01:22:18.897 --> 01:22:21.024
- Let me go!
- The roof's collapsing!

835
01:22:21.191 --> 01:22:24.695
- Somebody save my baby!
- The roof's about to collapse!

836
01:22:24.903 --> 01:22:26.238
Look! Up there!

837
01:22:32.828 --> 01:22:34.663
Save my baby, please!

838
01:22:58.395 --> 01:22:59.521
No!

839
01:23:07.279 --> 01:23:11.283
- It's okay. Your baby's fine.
- Oh, my baby!

840
01:23:12.326 --> 01:23:15.245
God bless you, Spider-Man.
Bless you.

841
01:23:15.454 --> 01:23:17.206
Don't let him get away!

842
01:23:17.414 --> 01:23:20.667
Hold it! You're under arrest.
I'm taking you in.

843
01:23:20.834 --> 01:23:24.171
Oh, my God, there's somebody
still up there!

844
01:23:25.631 --> 01:23:26.965
I'm going.

845
01:23:28.634 --> 01:23:31.678
- I'll be here when you get back.
- Not coming back.

846
01:23:32.095 --> 01:23:33.222
Go! Go!

847
01:23:42.147 --> 01:23:43.857
Where are you?

848
01:23:45.901 --> 01:23:47.486
Where are you?

849
01:23:52.866 --> 01:23:55.244
I'm gonna get you out of here!

850
01:23:57.829 --> 01:23:59.331
It's okay.

851
01:24:06.380 --> 01:24:08.966
You're pathetically predictable.

852
01:24:09.132 --> 01:24:11.051
Like a moth to the flame.

853
01:24:11.927 --> 01:24:14.388
What about my generous proposal?

854
01:24:15.430 --> 01:24:18.267
Are you in or are you out?

855
01:24:18.475 --> 01:24:24.398
- It's you who's out. Out of your mind.
- Wrong answer.

856
01:24:24.815 --> 01:24:26.316
Oh, great.

857
01:25:04.980 --> 01:25:07.774
No one says no to me!

858
01:25:15.115 --> 01:25:18.535
- M.J., will you stop goofing around?
- Harry, relax.

859
01:25:21.038 --> 01:25:22.289
He's here.

860
01:25:23.081 --> 01:25:24.583
Are you ready?

861
01:25:26.418 --> 01:25:29.087
Aunt May. I'm sorry I'm late.

862
01:25:29.296 --> 01:25:32.382
Work was murder.
I picked up a fruitcake.

863
01:25:32.591 --> 01:25:36.011
Thank you, Mr. Osborn.
We're so glad you could come.

864
01:25:36.261 --> 01:25:38.972
Who is this lovely young lady?

865
01:25:39.139 --> 01:25:43.435
I'd like you to meet my father.
Dad, this is Mary Jane Watson.

866
01:25:43.644 --> 01:25:46.313
I've been looking forward
to meeting you.

867
01:25:46.522 --> 01:25:50.234
- Happy Thanksgiving, sir.
- Now, where is Peter?

868
01:25:50.400 --> 01:25:52.778
He'd better remember
that cranberry sauce.

869
01:25:58.534 --> 01:26:02.120
Oh, that's weird.
I didn't know he was here.

870
01:26:05.123 --> 01:26:06.625
Peter?

871
01:26:14.675 --> 01:26:16.385
Is that you?

872
01:26:21.849 --> 01:26:26.019
How strange. There's nobody here.

873
01:26:32.484 --> 01:26:36.947
- Bit of a slob, isn't he?
- All brilliant men are.

874
01:27:09.563 --> 01:27:12.191
- Hey, everyone.
- Oh, Peter!

875
01:27:12.357 --> 01:27:14.109
It's a jungle out there.

876
01:27:14.276 --> 01:27:18.197
Had to beat an old lady with a stick
to get these Cranberries.

877
01:27:18.655 --> 01:27:21.491
Thank you.
Now then, everybody sit down...

878
01:27:21.658 --> 01:27:23.243
and we can say grace.

879
01:27:26.788 --> 01:27:28.540
Here we go.

880
01:27:35.506 --> 01:27:37.841
- There we are.
- It looks delicious.

881
01:27:41.637 --> 01:27:43.931
Will you do the honors?

882
01:27:55.609 --> 01:27:58.862
Why, Peter, you're bleeding.

883
01:28:01.698 --> 01:28:07.037
I stepped off a curb and got clipped
by one of those bike messengers.

884
01:28:07.204 --> 01:28:08.747
Well, let me see.

885
01:28:08.956 --> 01:28:10.457
Oh, my goodness.

886
01:28:10.707 --> 01:28:13.126
- That looks awful.
- No, it's nothing.

887
01:28:13.293 --> 01:28:16.421
I'll get the first-aid kit.
Then we'll say grace.

888
01:28:16.630 --> 01:28:21.927
This is the boys' first Thanksgiving
here, and we'll do things properly.

889
01:28:22.886 --> 01:28:25.973
How did you say that happened?

890
01:28:26.390 --> 01:28:28.100
Bike messenger.

891
01:28:28.308 --> 01:28:30.269
Knocked me down.

892
01:28:35.649 --> 01:28:39.319
- If you'll excuse me, I've got to go.
- Why?

893
01:28:40.237 --> 01:28:43.615
Something has come to my attention.

894
01:28:43.824 --> 01:28:45.075
Are you all right?

895
01:28:45.284 --> 01:28:48.787
I'm fine, just fine.
Thank you, Mrs. Parker. Everyone.

896
01:28:49.413 --> 01:28:51.790
- Enjoy the fruitcake.
- Dad!

897
01:28:53.959 --> 01:28:57.754
I planned this so you'd meet M.J.,
and now you have to leave?

898
01:28:57.963 --> 01:28:59.631
I've got to go.

899
01:28:59.965 --> 01:29:04.094
- This girl is important to me.
- Harry, please. Look at her.

900
01:29:04.303 --> 01:29:08.265
Think she's sniffing around
because she likes your personality?

901
01:29:08.515 --> 01:29:11.518
- What are you saying?
- Your mother was beautiful.

902
01:29:11.685 --> 01:29:17.107
They're all beautiful until they're
snarling after your money like wolves.

903
01:29:17.316 --> 01:29:18.567
You're wrong, Dad.

904
01:29:19.109 --> 01:29:22.321
A word to the not-so-wise
about your girlfriend:

905
01:29:22.487 --> 01:29:26.366
Do what you need to with her,
then broom her fast.

906
01:29:36.752 --> 01:29:39.296
Thanks for sticking up for me, Harry.

907
01:29:39.505 --> 01:29:42.466
- You heard?
- Everyone heard that creep.

908
01:29:42.674 --> 01:29:46.553
That creep is my father.
With luck, I'll be half of what he is.

909
01:29:46.803 --> 01:29:49.139
Shut up about stuff
you don't understand!

910
01:29:49.306 --> 01:29:50.974
Harry Osborn!

911
01:29:52.059 --> 01:29:54.102
I'm sorry, Aunt May.

912
01:29:57.064 --> 01:30:00.400
<i>Spider-Man is all but invincible.</i>

913
01:30:00.567 --> 01:30:03.695
<i>But Parker, we can destroy him.</i>

914
01:30:03.904 --> 01:30:05.239
I can't.

915
01:30:05.405 --> 01:30:08.408
<i>Betrayal must not be countenanced.</i>

916
01:30:08.659 --> 01:30:10.911
<i>Parker must be educated.</i>

917
01:30:13.080 --> 01:30:14.373
What do I do?

918
01:30:14.581 --> 01:30:18.669
<i>Instruct him in the matters
of loss and pain.</i>

919
01:30:18.836 --> 01:30:21.880
<i>Make him suffer.
Make him wish he were dead.</i>

920
01:30:22.130 --> 01:30:23.423
Yes?

921
01:30:23.590 --> 01:30:25.509
<i>And then Grant his wish.</i>

922
01:30:26.426 --> 01:30:27.719
But how?

923
01:30:27.928 --> 01:30:32.224
<i>The cunning warrior attacks
neither body nor mind.</i>

924
01:30:32.432 --> 01:30:33.600
Tell me how!

925
01:30:33.767 --> 01:30:35.936
<i>The heart, Osborn.</i>

926
01:30:36.186 --> 01:30:39.231
<i>First, we attack his heart.</i>

927
01:30:41.108 --> 01:30:44.611
Give us this day our daily bread,
and forgive us our trespasses...

928
01:30:44.820 --> 01:30:47.781
as we forgive those
who trespass against us.

929
01:30:48.031 --> 01:30:51.869
Lead us not into temptation,
but deliver us...

930
01:30:59.626 --> 01:31:02.171
Deliver us!

931
01:31:02.379 --> 01:31:03.755
Finish it!

932
01:31:04.047 --> 01:31:07.968
- Finish it!
- From evil!

933
01:31:13.682 --> 01:31:15.851
Two milligrams IV.

934
01:31:17.644 --> 01:31:18.896
Get the BP.

935
01:31:19.313 --> 01:31:22.900
Aunt May. Is she gonna be okay?
What happened?

936
01:31:23.108 --> 01:31:24.443
You have to leave.

937
01:31:24.610 --> 01:31:26.320
- What happened?
- Those eyes!

938
01:31:26.486 --> 01:31:30.574
Those horrible yellow eyes!

939
01:31:35.412 --> 01:31:37.956
He knows who I am.

940
01:32:21.917 --> 01:32:23.502
I'm sorry.

941
01:32:27.214 --> 01:32:29.675
- Will she be okay?
- She'll be fine.

942
01:32:29.842 --> 01:32:32.511
She's been sleeping all day.

943
01:32:33.512 --> 01:32:36.265
- Thanks for coming.
- Of course.

944
01:32:40.435 --> 01:32:43.355
How are you?
You okay about the other night?

945
01:32:43.522 --> 01:32:47.234
Yeah, I'm fine. I just felt bad
about leaving Aunt May.

946
01:32:47.442 --> 01:32:50.404
- Have you talked to Harry?
- He called me.

947
01:32:50.863 --> 01:32:53.031
I haven't called him back.

948
01:32:55.117 --> 01:32:56.827
The fact is...

949
01:32:57.995 --> 01:33:00.831
- I'm in love with somebody else.
- You are?

950
01:33:00.998 --> 01:33:03.208
At least I think I am.

951
01:33:04.877 --> 01:33:07.921
- It's not the time to talk about it.
- No. Go on.

952
01:33:08.088 --> 01:33:11.341
Would I know his name, this guy?

953
01:33:11.550 --> 01:33:14.428
You'll think I'm a little girl
with a crush.

954
01:33:14.595 --> 01:33:15.971
Trust me.

955
01:33:16.221 --> 01:33:17.472
It's funny.

956
01:33:19.474 --> 01:33:23.437
He's saved my life twice,
and I've never even seen his face.

957
01:33:23.604 --> 01:33:26.982
- Oh. Him.
- You're laughing at me.

958
01:33:27.191 --> 01:33:30.152
No, I understand.
He is extremely cool.

959
01:33:30.360 --> 01:33:34.656
But do you think it's true,
all the terrible things they say?

960
01:33:34.823 --> 01:33:37.743
Not Spider-Man,
not a chance in the world.

961
01:33:37.951 --> 01:33:39.578
I know him a little bit.

962
01:33:39.786 --> 01:33:42.664
I'm sort of his unofficial
photographer.

963
01:33:42.873 --> 01:33:46.001
- Has he mentioned me?
- Yeah.

964
01:33:46.335 --> 01:33:47.794
What'd he say?

965
01:33:48.378 --> 01:33:49.713
I said...

966
01:33:50.797 --> 01:33:55.093
He asked me what I thought about you.

967
01:33:56.011 --> 01:33:58.055
And what did you say?

968
01:33:58.764 --> 01:34:02.851
I said, "Spider-Man."

969
01:34:03.185 --> 01:34:08.065
I said, "The great thing about M.J..."

970
01:34:08.273 --> 01:34:09.816
is...

971
01:34:10.734 --> 01:34:13.987
when you look in her eyes...

972
01:34:16.532 --> 01:34:19.743
and she's looking back in yours...

973
01:34:20.744 --> 01:34:23.747
everything feels...

974
01:34:24.957 --> 01:34:26.792
not quite normal.

975
01:34:28.043 --> 01:34:29.837
Because you feel...

976
01:34:30.379 --> 01:34:32.005
stronger...

977
01:34:33.549 --> 01:34:37.177
and weaker at the same time.

978
01:34:38.220 --> 01:34:40.347
You feel excited...

979
01:34:41.223 --> 01:34:43.267
and at the same time...

980
01:34:43.892 --> 01:34:45.519
terrified.

981
01:34:47.855 --> 01:34:52.150
The truth is, you don't know
what you feel...

982
01:34:53.569 --> 01:34:57.197
except you know what kind of man
you want to be.

983
01:34:59.908 --> 01:35:01.785
It's as if you've...

984
01:35:02.411 --> 01:35:05.581
reached the unreachable...

985
01:35:07.165 --> 01:35:09.877
"...and you weren't ready for it."

986
01:35:13.338 --> 01:35:15.090
You said that?

987
01:35:15.883 --> 01:35:18.218
Well, something like that.

988
01:36:02.513 --> 01:36:04.014
Dad?

989
01:36:09.353 --> 01:36:11.438
Dad, is that you?

990
01:36:18.028 --> 01:36:19.530
What is it?

991
01:36:21.782 --> 01:36:26.787
You were right about M.J.
You're right about everything.

992
01:36:27.788 --> 01:36:30.499
She's in love with Peter.

993
01:36:30.791 --> 01:36:32.584
- Parker?
- Yeah.

994
01:36:32.751 --> 01:36:35.879
And how does he feel about her?

995
01:36:37.297 --> 01:36:39.842
He's loved her since the 4th grade.

996
01:36:40.801 --> 01:36:46.056
He pretends like he doesn't, but
there's no one Peter cares for more.

997
01:36:48.976 --> 01:36:50.727
I'm so sorry.

998
01:36:53.188 --> 01:36:56.650
I haven't always been there for you,
have I?

999
01:36:58.402 --> 01:37:01.613
You're busy. You're an important man.
I understand.

1000
01:37:01.780 --> 01:37:03.615
That's no excuse.

1001
01:37:04.616 --> 01:37:06.410
I'm proud of you.

1002
01:37:06.952 --> 01:37:11.832
I've lost sight of that somewhere.
But I'll make it up to you.

1003
01:37:11.999 --> 01:37:15.252
I'm going to rectify
certain inequities.

1004
01:37:29.391 --> 01:37:31.185
<i>Wake up, little spider.</i>

1005
01:37:31.351 --> 01:37:32.853
Wake up.

1006
01:37:34.188 --> 01:37:35.772
Go home, dear.

1007
01:37:35.981 --> 01:37:37.316
You look awful.

1008
01:37:37.524 --> 01:37:39.818
- And you look beautiful.
- Thank you.

1009
01:37:39.985 --> 01:37:43.322
- I don't like to leave you here.
- But I'm safe here.

1010
01:37:43.488 --> 01:37:46.200
- Can I do anything for you?
- You do too much.

1011
01:37:46.366 --> 01:37:51.914
College, a job, all this time with me.
You're not Superman, you know.

1012
01:37:52.664 --> 01:37:54.416
A smile. Finally.

1013
01:37:54.583 --> 01:37:58.921
Haven't seen one of those on your face
since Mary Jane was here.

1014
01:37:59.087 --> 01:38:01.381
You were supposed to be asleep.

1015
01:38:02.216 --> 01:38:06.970
You know, you were about 6 years old
when M.J.'s family moved in next door.

1016
01:38:07.179 --> 01:38:11.183
When she got out of the car,
and you saw her for the first time...

1017
01:38:11.391 --> 01:38:17.648
you grabbed me and said,
"Aunt May, is that an angel?"

1018
01:38:17.856 --> 01:38:21.401
- Gee, did I say that?
- You sure did.

1019
01:38:24.071 --> 01:38:26.823
Well, Harry's in love with her.

1020
01:38:27.032 --> 01:38:30.786
- She's still his girl.
- Well, isn't that up to her?

1021
01:38:30.994 --> 01:38:35.582
- She doesn't really know who I am.
- Because you won't let her.

1022
01:38:35.791 --> 01:38:38.919
You're so mysterious all the time.

1023
01:38:39.169 --> 01:38:41.922
Tell me, would it be so dangerous...

1024
01:38:42.130 --> 01:38:46.093
to let Mary Jane know
how much you care?

1025
01:38:46.552 --> 01:38:48.971
Everybody else knows.

1026
01:38:51.890 --> 01:38:53.183
I'll be right back.

1027
01:38:53.892 --> 01:38:55.185
But...

1028
01:39:02.526 --> 01:39:04.528
Come on, pick up.

1029
01:39:04.695 --> 01:39:07.990
- <i>Hey M.J.
- Hi. Sing your song at the beep.</i>

1030
01:39:09.032 --> 01:39:11.076
M.J., it's Peter. You there?

1031
01:39:11.368 --> 01:39:14.204
Hello? You there?

1032
01:39:14.705 --> 01:39:19.209
I'm just calling to check up on you.
Will you call me when you get in?

1033
01:39:19.376 --> 01:39:20.794
All right, well...

1034
01:39:21.211 --> 01:39:22.254
Don't...

1035
01:39:23.046 --> 01:39:25.257
Don't go up any dark alleys.

1036
01:39:25.465 --> 01:39:26.967
Hello?

1037
01:39:29.386 --> 01:39:33.098
<i>Can Spider-Man come out to play?</i>

1038
01:39:33.307 --> 01:39:35.058
Where is she?

1039
01:40:21.313 --> 01:40:22.981
- What is that?
- That's cool!

1040
01:40:23.190 --> 01:40:27.819
<i>The itsy-bitsy spider
Went up the water spout.</i>

1041
01:40:27.986 --> 01:40:32.157
<i>Down came the goblin
And took the spider out.</i>

1042
01:40:48.966 --> 01:40:50.717
Goblin, what have you done?

1043
01:41:33.177 --> 01:41:37.055
Spider-Man!
This is why only fools are heroes.

1044
01:41:37.431 --> 01:41:39.099
Because you never know...

1045
01:41:39.266 --> 01:41:44.021
when some lunatic will come along
with a sadistic choice:

1046
01:41:45.147 --> 01:41:47.774
Let die the woman you love...

1047
01:41:52.070 --> 01:41:57.159
or suffer the little children.

1048
01:41:59.536 --> 01:42:02.039
- Spider-Man!
- Save us!

1049
01:42:02.539 --> 01:42:04.833
Save us!

1050
01:42:05.125 --> 01:42:07.711
Make your choice, Spider-Man...

1051
01:42:07.920 --> 01:42:11.298
and see how a hero is rewarded.

1052
01:42:11.465 --> 01:42:13.550
Don't do it, Goblin!

1053
01:42:13.717 --> 01:42:16.637
We are who we choose to be.

1054
01:42:16.887 --> 01:42:19.640
- Now, choose!
- No!

1055
01:42:48.335 --> 01:42:49.920
Everybody stay still!

1056
01:42:59.429 --> 01:43:00.722
Ahoy up there!

1057
01:43:00.889 --> 01:43:03.851
We're gonna bring the barge
right under you.

1058
01:43:11.358 --> 01:43:15.487
- He's coming back!
- Listen. I need you to climb down.

1059
01:43:15.654 --> 01:43:17.155
- I can't.
- Yes, you can!

1060
01:43:22.244 --> 01:43:25.289
M.J., you can do it. You have to.

1061
01:43:25.455 --> 01:43:27.040
Trust me.

1062
01:43:28.542 --> 01:43:32.379
Hold on tight and go quickly.

1063
01:43:36.717 --> 01:43:38.760
- Hurry!
- I can't. I can't do it.

1064
01:43:38.969 --> 01:43:40.637
Hang on, Mary Jane!

1065
01:44:09.082 --> 01:44:11.710
- He's not gonna make it.
- He's gonna make it!

1066
01:44:21.595 --> 01:44:24.806
It's time to die.

1067
01:44:31.813 --> 01:44:35.651
- I got something for you!
- We ought to kick your ass!

1068
01:44:35.817 --> 01:44:39.238
Leave Spider-Man alone!
You'd pick on a guy saving kids?

1069
01:44:39.905 --> 01:44:43.408
You mess with Spidey,
you mess with New York!

1070
01:44:43.575 --> 01:44:47.120
You mess with one of us,
you mess with all of us!

1071
01:44:59.633 --> 01:45:01.426
Spider-Man, watch out!

1072
01:45:33.292 --> 01:45:37.546
Misery, misery, misery.
That's what you've chosen.

1073
01:45:38.463 --> 01:45:41.091
I offered you friendship...

1074
01:45:41.258 --> 01:45:43.135
and you spat in my face.

1075
01:46:34.228 --> 01:46:37.898
You've spun your last web, Spider-Man.

1076
01:46:38.065 --> 01:46:41.401
Had you not been so selfish,
your girlfriend's death...

1077
01:46:41.568 --> 01:46:43.237
would have been quick.

1078
01:46:43.403 --> 01:46:46.823
But now that you've really
pissed me off...

1079
01:46:47.074 --> 01:46:51.954
I'm gonna finish her
nice and slow.

1080
01:46:56.542 --> 01:46:58.585
M.J. and I...

1081
01:46:59.419 --> 01:47:02.714
we're gonna have a hell of a time.

1082
01:47:56.518 --> 01:47:58.061
Peter, stop!

1083
01:47:58.228 --> 01:48:00.689
Stop! It's me.

1084
01:48:09.656 --> 01:48:11.158
Mr. Osborn.

1085
01:48:11.325 --> 01:48:12.868
Thank God for you.

1086
01:48:13.076 --> 01:48:15.412
You killed those people
on that balcony.

1087
01:48:15.579 --> 01:48:18.624
The Goblin killed!
I had nothing to do with it!

1088
01:48:18.790 --> 01:48:20.542
Don't let him take me again.

1089
01:48:20.709 --> 01:48:22.753
I beg you. Protect me.

1090
01:48:22.920 --> 01:48:26.507
You tried to kill Aunt May.
You tried to kill Mary Jane.

1091
01:48:26.673 --> 01:48:28.175
But not you.

1092
01:48:28.842 --> 01:48:32.804
I tried to stop it.
But I couldn't stop it.

1093
01:48:33.013 --> 01:48:35.098
I would never hurt you.

1094
01:48:35.307 --> 01:48:37.226
I knew from the beginning...

1095
01:48:37.434 --> 01:48:40.354
if anything ever happened to me...

1096
01:48:40.521 --> 01:48:42.648
it was you I could count on.

1097
01:48:42.814 --> 01:48:46.193
You, Peter Parker, would save me,
and so you have.

1098
01:48:46.777 --> 01:48:48.612
Thank God for you.

1099
01:48:49.613 --> 01:48:51.031
Give me your hand.

1100
01:48:52.199 --> 01:48:55.619
Believe in me
as I believed in you.

1101
01:48:57.037 --> 01:48:59.831
I've been like a father to you.

1102
01:49:01.375 --> 01:49:03.043
Be a son to me now.

1103
01:49:04.837 --> 01:49:06.713
I have a father.

1104
01:49:07.464 --> 01:49:09.967
His name was Ben Parker.

1105
01:49:11.844 --> 01:49:13.303
Godspeed, Spider-Man.

1106
01:49:32.239 --> 01:49:33.740
Peter.

1107
01:49:36.076 --> 01:49:37.911
Don't tell Harry.

1108
01:50:09.610 --> 01:50:11.320
What have you done?

1109
01:50:11.486 --> 01:50:13.071
What have you done?!

1110
01:50:41.225 --> 01:50:43.268
I'm so sorry, Harry.

1111
01:50:44.186 --> 01:50:47.314
I know what it's like
to lose a father.

1112
01:50:49.483 --> 01:50:52.778
I didn't lose him.
He was stolen from me.

1113
01:50:54.363 --> 01:50:56.657
One day Spider-Man will pay.

1114
01:50:58.534 --> 01:51:01.662
I swear on my father's grave,
Spider-Man will pay.

1115
01:51:06.667 --> 01:51:08.502
Thank God for you, Peter.

1116
01:51:09.211 --> 01:51:11.672
You're the only family I have.

1117
01:51:36.196 --> 01:51:38.490
<i>No matter what I do...</i>

1118
01:51:38.657 --> 01:51:41.785
<i>no matter how hard I try...</i>

1119
01:51:42.369 --> 01:51:46.206
<i>the ones I love will always
be the ones who pay.</i>

1120
01:51:56.925 --> 01:51:59.261
You must miss him so much.

1121
01:52:00.220 --> 01:52:03.265
It's been so hard without him.

1122
01:52:06.185 --> 01:52:09.062
There's something
I've been wanting to tell you.

1123
01:52:10.856 --> 01:52:12.649
When I was up there...

1124
01:52:13.400 --> 01:52:16.195
and I thought I was gonna die...

1125
01:52:17.821 --> 01:52:21.658
there was only one person
who I was thinking of.

1126
01:52:22.951 --> 01:52:26.163
And it wasn't who I thought it'd be.

1127
01:52:27.623 --> 01:52:30.042
It was you, Pete.

1128
01:52:30.918 --> 01:52:32.794
I kept thinking:

1129
01:52:33.212 --> 01:52:36.006
"I hope I make it through this...

1130
01:52:37.466 --> 01:52:41.845
so I can see Peter Parker's face
one more time."

1131
01:52:43.222 --> 01:52:44.723
Really?

1132
01:52:45.098 --> 01:52:50.896
There's only one man
who's always been there for me...

1133
01:52:52.147 --> 01:52:54.107
who makes me feel...

1134
01:52:54.566 --> 01:52:58.278
like I'm more than I ever
thought I could be.

1135
01:53:00.405 --> 01:53:02.074
That I'm just...

1136
01:53:02.741 --> 01:53:04.243
me.

1137
01:53:05.327 --> 01:53:07.246
And that's okay.

1138
01:53:09.456 --> 01:53:10.916
The truth is...

1139
01:53:13.043 --> 01:53:14.837
I love you.

1140
01:53:16.964 --> 01:53:18.882
I love you so much, Peter.

1141
01:53:39.611 --> 01:53:44.366
<i>All I wanted was to tell her
how much I loved her.</i>

1142
01:53:44.533 --> 01:53:46.451
I can't...

1143
01:53:48.579 --> 01:53:50.122
You can't what?

1144
01:53:51.248 --> 01:53:52.708
Tell you...

1145
01:53:54.418 --> 01:53:58.755
everything.
I mean, there's so much to tell.

1146
01:53:59.840 --> 01:54:03.760
Yeah. There's so much to tell.

1147
01:54:04.678 --> 01:54:06.638
I want you to know...

1148
01:54:07.055 --> 01:54:09.725
that I will always be there
for you.

1149
01:54:09.933 --> 01:54:13.896
I will always be there
to take care of you.

1150
01:54:14.897 --> 01:54:16.899
I promise you that.

1151
01:54:20.194 --> 01:54:22.487
I will always be your friend.

1152
01:54:25.407 --> 01:54:27.284
Only a friend...

1153
01:54:28.160 --> 01:54:29.703
Peter Parker?

1154
01:54:31.872 --> 01:54:34.708
That's all I have to give.

1155
01:55:01.068 --> 01:55:03.737
<i>Whatever life holds in store for me...</i>

1156
01:55:03.904 --> 01:55:06.782
I will never forget these words:

1157
01:55:06.990 --> 01:55:12.037
<i>"With great power
comes great responsibility."</i>

1158
01:55:12.204 --> 01:55:14.456
<i>This is my gift.</i>

1159
01:55:14.623 --> 01:55:16.750
<i>My curse.</i>

1160
01:55:17.251 --> 01:55:19.169
<i>Who am I?</i>

1161
01:55:19.545 --> 01:55:20.921
<i>I'm Spider-Man.</i>

1162
02:01:10.812 --> 02:01:11.855
Subtitles By cHiBcHaKaN

1163
